<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiglath-pileser III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 745–727 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tiglath-pileser III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> from 745 to 727 BCE and the architect of the Neo-Assyrian imperial system. He reorganised provincial administration into smaller units under royal governors, created a standing army, and greatly expanded the use of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">mass deportation</a>. Accounts of the Assyrian Empire treat his reforms as the foundation of Assyria's economy, military power and governance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-iii.jpg" alt="Tiglath-pileser III" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tilglath_pileser_iii.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
